    "description": "IQAir builds the HealthPro Plus for people who cannot afford leaky filtration, and its design reflects that. Air passes through a coarse pre-filter, a carbon and pelletized gas-phase stage for odors and chemicals, and finally a HyperHEPA stage that IQAir rates for particles down to 0.003 microns. Mold spores are hundreds to thousands of times larger than that, so they are well within its range. Just as important, the housing is built so air cannot sneak around the filters, a weak point in many cheaper machines. Owners with mold allergies and asthma tend to be the most enthusiastic reviewers, and the unit has a long record in hospitals and clinics. The drawbacks are price and size. It costs roughly $900 to $1,200 at the time of writing, and it is a substantial box that suits a living room or finished basement better than a nightstand. Filter replacement is also pricey, though the main HEPA stage lasts several years in normal use. If the budget allows and someone in the house reacts to spores, this is the safest choice."
