    "description": "The Core 600S is the large-room model in Levoit's popular Core line, and it brings a lot of airflow for the money. Levoit lists a clean air delivery rate of about 410 cubic feet per minute, which is enough for several air changes an hour in a typical living room or bedroom suite. A laser particle sensor feeds the auto mode, and the app shows air quality history, so you can see whether spore and dust levels spike when the basement door is open or the dehumidifier is off. Levoit sells several replacement filters for the 600S, including one marketed for mold and toxin absorption with a heavier carbon blend. Owners commonly mention the quiet sleep mode and the low price compared with premium brands. The weak points are minor: the cylinder needs a foot or so of open space around it to draw air evenly, and the smart features add little if you just set it to auto and forget it. For most households dealing with mild mold-related allergies, it is the best value at its size."
